5. In the said rules, in rule 6, in sub-rule (1),—
(1) in clause (d), the words, “or pre-packed or imported” shall be omitted;

(ii) in clause (e), for the words commencing with “and the price in rupees and paisa”, and ending with “(d)
MRP Rs. & xx.xx(inclusive of all taxes):”, the words “in Indian currency:” shall be substituted;

(iil) after sub-rule (10), the following sub-rule shall be inserted, namely: —
“(11) The unit sale price shall be declared as—

(i) “Rs.__ per g” for pre-packaged commodities with net quantity of commodity less than one
kilogram;

(ii) “Rs. per kg” for pre-packaged commodities with net quantity of commodity more or
equal to one kilogram;

(iii) “Rs. per cm” for pre-packaged commodities with net length of the commodity less than
one meter;

(iv) “Rs. per meter” for pre-packaged commodities with net length of the commodity more or
equal to one meter;

(v) “Rs. per number”;

(vi) “Rs. per ml” for pre-packaged commodities with net volume of the commodity less than
one litre;

(vii) “Rs.__ per litre” for pre-packaged commodities with net volume of the commodity more or
equal to one litre.”.
